--------------------------- Changelog -----------------------------

1.0.d - UNRELEASED
Added - Two fishing ships with their own hulls: the Stigmata-class Harpoon Tug, a fast midline destroyer as heavy as a small cruiser, with a 180° omni shield, a fighter bay and a built-in harpoon mount, and the Reliquary-class LYNE Tender, a slow midline carrier cruiser with one fighter bay, meant for a built-in wing of LYNE drones
Added - The Stigmata-class Harpoon Tug has a built-in Tug Drive Field: each one in your fleet (not mothballed) adds 1 to the fleet's maximum burn level, and the first adds 20% campaign acceleration, each further one half the previous bonus (+10%, +5%, ...). It does nothing while Sustained Burn is on
Added - The Stigmata-class Harpoon Tug has a built-in Tug Harpoon: 2 charges, one regained every 12 seconds, 400 kinetic damage (none to friendly ships) and 900 range. A harpoon that hits a ship's hull or armour, friend, foe or wreck, tethers it for 20 seconds at the distance it struck from: a taut tether drags both ships, the lighter one more. A harpoon that hits a shield glances off at reduced speed, at most twice. Firing again lets go, without launching another harpoon or spending a charge. The tether is drawn as a thin rope that flies straight out with the harpoon, flashes into place at 80% opacity when it bites, and floats loose and loops when slack. Both ends of the rope fade to half opacity over their last 50 pixels. After a shot the launcher swings smoothly back to its resting angle
Added - The Reliquary-class LYNE Tender carries one built-in wing of five LYNE drones: unarmed, very fast salvage drones
Added - While a Reliquary is in a battle, enemy fighters it can salvage leave wrecks 75% of the time instead of half, and their wrecks hold for 30 seconds instead of about 10. Fighters the Reliquary launches never leave a wreck. Its LYNE drones fly out to wrecks within 8,000 units, tow them back and land with them in the forward bay. Each salvaged fighter goes into the Reliquary's store, up to 10, and is restored in combat at its wing's refit time; the drones leave wrecks alone while the store is full. The store stays with the ship between battles and is emptied if the ship leaves your fleet
Note - Fighters recovered in a simulator battle never reach the store
Added - The Reliquary's system, Salvage Launch, sends out every restored fighter in its store at once, in wings of their usual size. They fight as normal fighters, come back to the store to rearm or when fighters are called in, and are gone if destroyed. AI-flown Reliquaries launch once two fighters are ready, or all of them, with an enemy in reach
Added - In combat, a Reliquary you fly lists its recovered fighters above the ship display, where terrain effects show: how many of each type are ready or still being restored
Added - In the refit screen, a Reliquary's recovered fighters show as extra locked fighter bays, one per wing, up to four, and the Salvage Bays tooltip lists them with their restoration
Added - "Recovered fighters" under the refit screen's Additional Options on each Reliquary: lists its stored fighters and discards the ones you don't want. Discarded fighters are gone for good and give no LPC
Added - "Reliquary recovered fighter capacity" setting in Fishing Equipment (10 by default)
Added - "Reliquary fighter wreck chance (%)" setting in Fishing Equipment (75% by default)
Added - AI-flown Stigmatas harpoon enemy ships to drag them into the guns of nearby friendly ships, and hold the harpoon with no friends near. They prefer ships with shields down or turned away, that are overloaded, damaged or running and light enough to drag. They never fire into a shield facing them, past a friendly ship or into any other raised shield in the way, and let go of a tether that is no longer worth holding. Once hooked, they drag their catch toward friendly ships and away from enemies and hold it once it is within friendly guns, firing the Haul Drive when the catch is heavy or pulls away, and to escape when badly damaged. They also hook friendly ships that are swarmed, or outnumbered while overloaded or badly damaged, and drag them back to friendly lines. When swarmed they hold the harpoon, and one towing lets go and runs, firing the Haul Drive
Added - The Stigmata's system, the Haul Drive, raises the ship's mass up to 2.5 times for 5 seconds, with +150% acceleration, +150% turn acceleration, +50% turn rate and +50% top speed, for hauling a tethered catch. Longer flames and a long trail of dark smoke while it runs. 3 charges, one regained every 20 seconds
Fixed - Fleets already offering a quest, or whose commander is marked important for a mission, no longer take on a fishing job as well
Changed - The marker beside a fleet whose fishing job you have accepted is now a steady gold instead of pulsing; offers still pulse light blue
Changed - Codex entries known only from range data show no fish icon, in the list or on their page, until you catch the fish
Fixed - A fish's codex list icon no longer stays blank until its art has been shown elsewhere, such as on its codex page
Changed - The Retrieval Head, Fanned Array and Lifting Rig are no longer sold or given as rewards. They come with the fishing ships, which add a second equipment slot to their rig while they are in your fleet. Copies you already own are kept
Added - After the tutorial, the Fisherman has a treasure rumour for a nearby system in place of the free lead, and shows the system on the map as he offers it. He has lost a golden chest there: it can come up in the catch window on lamp catches in that system (30% each, and certain on the 4th, then every 2nd, until taken). Bring back the compass inside for the Glitter Lens schematic plus the fish and credits to buy it. The rumour's bycatch boost lasts until you return the compass, then another two months once you buy the lens; an intel entry tracks buying it, the lens goes on your Outfitter shopping list, and his Outfitter option is highlighted until you buy it
Added - If you lose the Fisherman's compass, tell him: he remembers where it was sold, checks your storage, and if it is gone for good he pays you anyway
Added - Once the Glitter Lens is built, the Fisherman passes on a request from an old crewman: a captain hunting an epic (never the Dopefish) in a nearby system with no markets, whose Breach Lights have failed; the system shows on the map as he asks. His fleet carries the fishing-job marker, light blue until you have met him and yellow after, never takes on a fishing job of its own, and once met stays on the map. Keep your lights on within 6,000 units of the star's surface for 15 seconds without a break to find the epic, then harpoon it. Either way he gives you a Stigmata-class Harpoon Tug, with its second Harpoon slot and the Retrieval Head; landing the epic also pays a harpoon module schematic and three range-data entries
Added - Report back to the Fisherman afterwards for a word on hunting epics and the Needle Sensor schematic. An intel entry tracks building it, the sensor goes on your Outfitter shopping list, and his Outfitter option is highlighted until you buy it
Added - With the Needle Sensor built, the Fisherman sends you after a wounded epic circling a planet about 1,000 units out in a nearby empty system, never the captain's system or species; the planet shows on the map as he offers it. Its Needle Sensor ripples trace its circle. It swims at half speed once woken and is the only one of its species in that system while you hunt it. A hunt that loses it, or putting your Breach Lights out while it is awake, sends it back to the planet. Landing it pays range data on an epic. He then sends you to a drunk in the bar of an independent Core world, highlighted there, who will trade his old Reliquary-class LYNE Tender for three epic fish, or two if you spend a story point haggling; it brings a second Drone Core slot and the Lifting Rig. Show the Fisherman the ship for a last word
Added - After the Reliquary, the Fisherman tells you to improve your gear and listen for rumours. Landing your first legendary completes it, and he hands over a Monstrance-class Breach Trawler, with a second Lens Array slot and the Fanned Array. The Lifting Rig and the Salvage Trawl cannot share the rig. From then on a "Hunting the legendary fish" intel lists every legendary: question marks until you hear of one, the name its teller used after that, and its real name once caught
Added - Report each legendary you land to the Fisherman, one conversation at a time: the option comes back highlighted in his menu while another is waiting. The first completes "Listen for rumours" and pays the Monstrance; the next three pay the Stigmata, Reliquary and Monstrance blueprints. A legendary reported before his earlier jobs are done ends them and pays what they would have paid
Changed - Legendary rumour intel shows the name the teller used. The bar spacer's stories that name nothing go by a name from the story until you catch the fish
Added - "Surfaced lamp-fish speed (%)" setting in Ruptures & Exploration: the speed of fish that surface in your Breach Lights, as a percentage of their normal speed (100% by default). Lower it to make them easier to chase down
Changed - Ordinary fish now surface as soon as your Breach Lights reach them and swim in their own style until caught or gone; epic and legendary fish still stay hidden until harpooned. Turn this off with "Surface fish in breach lights" in the Ruptures & Exploration settings, or turn on "Straight lamp-fish movement" to have surfaced fish swim the old straight course with a gentle weave instead of their own style
Changed - The Tracking Gimbal also follows fish your Breach Lights have surfaced, and the tracking upgrade keeps them visible and in reach after the beam moves on
Changed - Fight Night's fee option now reads "Take the rewards." and lists the rewards in its tooltip
Changed - Every equipment module costs one price tier more (25,000 to 45,000 credits), and none can be paid for with common fish alone
Added - Glitter Lens, a Lens Array module that doubles the chance of bycatch on catches made under Breach Lights. Its schematic comes only from the Fisherman's treasure rumour, never from job or distress rewards
Changed - The Neutrino Lens only shows its spikes while the Breach Lights are on as well as the Neutrino Detector
Removed - The Breach Coupler is withdrawn for now: it is no longer sold or awarded, and one already fitted does nothing; ROD drones fish ruptures only
Changed - Every epic fish now comes up only under Breach Lights; ruptures fished with the ROD no longer hold them
Changed - Epic fish are now hunted in two stages: they drift slowly until a harpoon hit inside a lit Breach Light beam wakes them, then raise a one-charge shield that never comes back and swim more erratically, staying in view with your lights off; one that gets more than 3,000 units away drifts off and fades, with a notice that it was lost, and an awake epic is gone once you leave the system. Only the harpoon lands one: ROD drones leave epics alone
Fixed - Epic and legendary shields now fade out with the fish when it dives, instead of staying on screen while it is out of reach
Added - Version Checker support: update notices, plus the changelog and direct download for LunaLib's update screen and mod managers such as triOS

Outfitter
Fixed - The Outfitter no longer opens on a locked shelf with an empty list and no category selected, which happened on every visit before the Breach Lights were unlocked
Fixed - Undoing a purchase made on another tab now brings that item's shelf to the front instead of describing one row while highlighting none
Fixed - Buying a module that fits both rigs now clears its mark on the other rig's shelf, and the route planner no longer lists the same module twice
Fixed - Equipment with no fish price now says it is not for sale, instead of showing a price with a FIT button that does nothing
Changed - The Equipment category tabs follow the same rig order as the Upgrades tabs
Adjusted - The shopping-list dot in Outfitter rows sits centred between the row's edge and its name
Changed - The Equipment help text no longer refers to a single-use marker that was never drawn; equipment consumed on use says so in its description

Text and UI
Adjusted - Clearer fishing settings and AddFish help

Development
Adjusted - AddFish accepts a fish ID or full name, followed by quantity, quality and coherence; quantity defaults to 1 and names autocomplete

1.0.c

Quests and payments
Fixed - A camp fleet that loses a fight to you gives up the rupture and leaves, instead of holding it until destroyed
Fixed - Job intel names the market and star system to deliver to, and switches to "Return to" once you have the catch; a cleared camp job points back to the fisher once the proof is aboard
Fixed - Automatic job and Outfitter payments no longer consume legendary fish.
Removed - Disabled legendary tribute at Kanta's Den pending dialogue replacement.

Fleet interactions
Changed - Contract hunters respond less often to single harpoon hits, but may pursue unpaid repair bills or fleeing after identification following a dark hit. Paying the fine calls them off.
Changed - Crews with unpaid repair bills now report you to local patrols instead of chasing you. All patrols in the system demand payment on sight until the fine is paid.

Crablobab
Added - Crablobab sells Party Horn after acquiring Celebration Charges, followed by Crab Fanfare. Both replace the catch sound and can be previewed before purchase and selected in the Outfitter.

Equipment
Added - Neutrino Lens module for the Lens Array. Shows rare, epic and legendary patterns as rarity-coloured Neutrino Detector spikes. Grants the detector if missing.
Fixed - Needle Sensor ripples are larger, brighter and visible at greater zoom distances.

Treasure
Added - Uncommon fishing chests have a 25% chance to contain unknown range data alongside normal loot, including with the Lifting Rig.
Changed - Recovered treasure now has aligned quantities; range data displays as "Range data: <fish>".

Harpoon
Adjusted - Harpoons hitting shields no longer play the catch sound.

Legendaries
Removed - Failed Quorum catches no longer spawn 12 extra decoys.
Fixed - Dormant epics and legendaries now leave trails under breach lights.
Fixed - Loading saves with Lantern Jack surfaced in the current system no longer crashes.
Fixed - Reduced performance cost of epic and legendary trails under breach lights.
Fixed - Legendary floating text use shield or mote colour instead of a generic UI highlight
Added - Lantern Jack now coils for 0.3 seconds within 300 units of a mote, then dashes through it to feed (also: added vfx)

Aquarium
Fixed - Corrected aquarium swimming orientation for 13 species, including Dopefish and several legendaries.

1.0.b

General
Added - Temporary industry image

Fisherman
Fixed - Nearby settlements no longer prevent the Fisherman from approaching you for the tutorial
Fixed - Finishing the Fisherman's "Why a fish?" questions no longer shows an empty Continue before "You could have told me this before I started."
Fixed - Fisherman tutorial lessons no longer send you to systems with a neutron star
Adjusted - The Fisherman's first lesson now points at the rupture closest to him
Added - Selling fish to the Fisherman can unpack crates again after using "Pack into crates"
Fixed - Hovering the "Pack into crates" button in the Fisherman sale screen no longer repeats the click sound
Fixed - Undo in the Fisherman's range data shop takes back every purchase in sequence, newest first, like the Outfitter
Adjusted - Buncha dialogue
Fixed - "Set autopilot" on tutorial and chart request intel now targets a visiting Fisherman in your current system instead of a boat elsewhere

Fish
Added - New portraits for 16 fish that had placeholders until now
Added - Dopefish, a rare Epic catch that barely moves and is very easy to land
Fixed - System fish counts no longer include a species that never spawns there, which made a full system show 16 species
Fixed - A star system never offers more than 15 species; a legendary in a full system temporarily takes one of those slots

Legendaries
Added - Lantern Jack's lure call now plays a distress-call sound
Added - Harpoons deflected by a legendary's shield play a varied shield-hit sound
Added - Epic fish leave a fainter purple version of the legendary trail under breach lights
Adjusted - Buried and diving legendaries and epics no longer leave a trail
Added - A foghorn sounds when a legendary haunt starts and ends

Outfitter
Added - Hovering an Outfitter fish count shows the species of that rarity aboard

Cargo and items
Fixed - Fish, crate and pile tooltips only show their right-click hints for fish in your fleet's cargo, not in markets, storage or selection screens
Adjusted - Fish art on crate labels in cargo is drawn sharper
Adjusted - Tooltips across most items
Fixed - Fish, crates and piles sold to a market now disappear when its stock refreshes

Codex
Added - Codex pages of caught fish show a size distribution chart with your best and latest catch

1.0.a
Added - Initial Mod Release

General
Adjusted - Release downloads leave out development tools, libraries and source files
Adjusted - Rewrote fishing settings descriptions to explain their effects and limits more clearly

Development
